# Build output
bin/
build/bin/
dist-installers/

# The renderer is built into frontend/dist and embedded with go:embed.
#
# The directory is ignored, but `.gitkeep` is committed: `//go:embed all:frontend/dist` fails to
# compile when the pattern matches nothing, so without a tracked file `go build ./...` and
# `go test ./...` would both fail on a clean clone, before anything had a chance to run. The `all:`
# prefix is what makes a dotfile count.
frontend/dist/*
!frontend/dist/.gitkeep

frontend/node_modules/
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Wails regenerates these; nothing under frontend/src imports them (the bridge uses Call.ByName).
frontend/bindings/

# Secrets. Carried over from the 2.x repository: a signing identity or a provider token that lands
# here is published the moment the repository is public.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.mobileprovision

# "secrets" as a word, not as a prefix. The unanchored `secrets*` this replaces also matched
# `backend/security/secretscan.go` — the secret scanner's own source — and silently kept it out of
# the repository, where it would have been missing from every clone.
secrets
secrets.*
secrets-*
secrets_*

# Per-developer configuration, never shared
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor and IDE state. Per developer by definition: a committed .idea/ makes everyone else's
# inspections, run configurations and module paths change under them.
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# macOS
.DS_Store
